               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 21-year-old male patient, admitted on 05/02/2010 with a two-day history of progressive right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically consistent with acute appendicitis. On admission, physical examination revealed rebound tenderness at McBurney's point. Blood tests confirmed leukocytosis with neutrophilia. Abdominal ultrasound supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis without perforation. The patient underwent laparoscopic emergency appendectomy on the same day without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, he received intravenous antibiotics, analgesics, and fluid replacement. Wound healing was uneventful. Vital signs remained stable throughout the stay. The patient was mobilized early and discharged home on 07/02/2010 in good general condition. Please arrange follow-up in approximately two weeks for wound inspection and removal of any remaining sutures. Do not hesitate to contact me with any questions.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
